---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Observability | Christopher Fickess"
  description="Live signal from the infrastructure and code behind this site"
  current="observability"
  pageTitle="Observability"
>
  <section class="observability-page">
    <header class="observability-head">
      <p class="kicker">Observability</p>
      <h2>Live Signal</h2>
      <p class="observability-intro">The same discipline I apply at work, pointed at my own stuff: real data instead of a static claim that everything's fine. Nothing here is staged.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="obs-section">
      <h3 class="obs-section-title">Uptime</h3>
      <div class="obs-stub-card">
        <p>Not wired up yet. Checking "is this reachable" from a visitor's own browser doesn't actually measure uptime (it mostly measures their network and gets blocked by CORS on most sites) - the honest way to do this is a real monitoring service running independent checks on a schedule. This section is ready to connect to one (UptimeRobot's free tier, or similar) once that's set up, for:</p>
        <ul class="obs-stub-list">
          <li>This portfolio site</li>
          <li>The three practice sites linked from <a href="/projects/">Projects</a></li>
          <li>Starlight, the homelab behind the featured project</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="obs-section">
      <h3 class="obs-section-title">GitHub Contributions</h3>
      <p class="obs-section-sub">The last year of commit activity, fetched live from GitHub's public contribution calendar.</p>
      <div id="github-contributions" class="obs-contrib-wrap">
        <p class="obs-loading">Loading contribution graph&hellip;</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="obs-section">
      <h3 class="obs-section-title">GitHub Activity</h3>
      <p class="obs-section-sub">Most recently pushed repos, fetched live from GitHub's public API.</p>
      <div id="github-activity" class="obs-activity-list">
        <p class="obs-loading">Loading recent activity&hellip;</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="obs-section">
      <h3 class="obs-section-title">GitLab Activity</h3>
      <p class="obs-section-sub">Most recently active projects, fetched live from GitLab's public API.</p>
      <div id="gitlab-activity" class="obs-activity-list">
        <p class="obs-loading">Loading recent activity&hellip;</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>
    import "../../scripts/github-contributions.js";
    import "../../scripts/observability.js";
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
